  "verbalization": "Carmustine, a chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the treatment of B-cell neoplasms through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Carmustine may exert its effects on B-cell neoplasms via a chain of interactions involving bleomycin and subsequent pathways. Path_34936 links Carmustine to lymphosarcoma, which is associated with acalabrutinib, a B-cell neoplasm target. Path_34937 and Path_34938 connect Carmustine to diffuse large B-cell lymphoma of the central nervous system and plasmablastic lymphoma, both of which are classified as B-cell neoplasms. These pathways involve bleomycin, which is indicated as a treatment for these conditions and is known to have a role in B-cell neoplasms. The final scores indicate a moderate level of support for the relationship, but the evidence is indirect and relies on the indication links rather than direct mechanistic evidence. The integration of these paths suggests that Carmustine may influence B-cell neoplasms through a chain of interactions involving bleomycin, though the exact mechanism remains unclear.",
